Conclusion: PASS for clean Unitree driver shutdown and restart under the validated network configuration.

## Physical Ethernet disconnect and reconnect

Before disconnect:

- eth0 connected
- `lidar-phase2-test` active
- route to 192.168.1.62 through eth0
- cloud approximately 11.95 Hz

On cable removal:

- eth0 reported NO-CARRIER
- cloud publication stopped as expected

The first reconnect attempt selected `netplan-eth0` because `lidar-phase2-test` still had autoconnect disabled. DHCP failed, `192.168.1.2` disappeared, and the LiDAR route moved to wlan0. This was a machine-profile selection failure, not a driver failure.

After setting `lidar-phase2-test` autoconnect to yes with priority 100 and disabling autoconnect for `netplan-eth0`, the test was repeated. On unplug/replug:

- eth0 automatically recovered carrier
- NetworkManager automatically selected `lidar-phase2-test`
- 192.168.1.2/24 automatically returned
- route became `192.168.1.62 dev eth0 src 192.168.1.2`
- ping passed at approximately 0.15 ms
- the same already-running driver resumed publication
- cloud returned at approximately 11.95 Hz
- IMU returned at approximately 251 Hz

Conclusion: PASS for automatic physical Ethernet disconnect/reconnect recovery with the validated Pi profile. The driver becomes silent while transport is unavailable and resumes from the existing process when the route returns.

## Pi reboot persistence

After reboot, no manual `ip addr add`, `ip route add`, or `nmcli connection up` command was run.

Observed network restoration:

- active profile `lidar-phase2-test` on eth0
- IPv4 192.168.1.2/24
- route `192.168.1.62 dev eth0 src 192.168.1.2`
- ping 3/3 successful, approximately 0.149 ms average

After sourcing the corrected focused build and launching the Unitree driver:

- `/unilidar/cloud` approximately 11.95 to 11.97 Hz
- `/unilidar/imu` approximately 249 to 250 Hz
- observed cloud width 5152

Conclusion: PASS for persistent LiDAR Ethernet configuration across reboot, automatic network restoration, driver operation after reboot, and cloud/IMU publication after reboot. Complete repository-managed robot bring-up remains a later deployment phase; the driver was launched after sourcing the focused build.

